A||||11||GodSend||Playstation Pics.||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||10-15-2001||11:20 PM||||Well, the playstation project is almost done.  I had to change my plans a little bit.  I installed a PSone into the former glove box.  The unit is so small its unbelievable.  The PSOne unit uses an external transformer for power, which means that they sell a plug in adapter for it for a 12v application.<P>I installed an AUX power plug under the dash.  I also installed 2 PlayStation controller extenders.  I will be perminatly mounting them to Aus Sub Box where you would normally find the lighter.  I did this so you can easily plug and unplug controllers.<P>I picked up the 4 inch LCD screen from partsexpress.  It actually is a pretty good size, and the resolution is great.  <P>Here is a cost run down.<P>PlayStation 139$ Canadian<BR>Extra Controller 9.99$ Canadian<BR>COntroller Extenders 30.00$ Canadian<BR>12v PSone adapter 14.99$ Canadian<BR>Aux 12v Power Plug 9.99$ Canadian<BR>Playstation Mod Chip (to play copied games) 45$ installed Canadian<BR>LCD Screeb 99$ American.<BR>Indash PPI EQ with Aux Inputs 200$ Canadian Used.<P>The trim piece for the playstation on monitor will be changed to abs plastic soon.  I got really sick right in the middle of the project and needed to get my dash back together, so I rushed the trim (its actually a template I just covered with some fabric for now).<P>And the pics..<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.globalserve.net/~kesik/ps1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.globalserve.net/~kesik/ps2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.globalserve.net/~kesik/ps3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.globalserve.net/~kesik/ps4.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.globalserve.net/~kesik/ps5.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.globalserve.net/~kesik/ps6.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||72vinman||10-15-2001||11:33 PM||||That looks pretty cool. I would love to get a closer look at that. Why don't you come down to the GTA Fiero club meeting tomorrow and let us try a game or two. Let me know, Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000002||falconhulk||10-16-2001||08:09 AM||||Hey do your door speakers take a beating from passengers?  Seems a little dangerous having open speakers, especially ones that stick out.  Do you have them on the drivers side also?  If so you must be tiny.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GodSend||10-16-2001||10:23 AM||||6 feet tall, 180 pounds.  No problems here.  90% of the time its only me in the car, so I am always careful of my stuff.  I do have grills for the speakers, but for some reason the grills for the 8's are a little too big.. *shrug*.<P>There are no space problems.  They only eat up 4 inchs of leg room, which is not much considering. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||10-16-2001||11:06 AM||||Nice PSOne install... I'm planning mine a little different.  I'd like to go with a slightly larger screen (center it in the former map-pocket) to fill the space, then attache the PSOne (probably with velcro) to the lower footwell on the passenger side.  That way I can take it in and out to use it at home too.  I want to keep the system "open" to allow for a future DVD/PS2 and/or Automotive VCR.  Looks great- shouldn't you have GranToursimo 1 or 2 in there?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
